      },
      "source": [
        "# Logical Entailment Reasoning Agent\n",
        "\n",
        "**Pipeline:** natural-language knowledge base → internal representation → *classical* reasoning engine → `True` / `False`.\n",
        "No generative AI takes part in any decision.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Engine | Used for | Classical techniques |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| NL parser + forward chaining | RuleTaker-style facts and rules | unification-style matching, forward chaining, stratified negation-as-failure, strong negation |\n",
        "| FOL parser + resolution | FOLIO-style first-order logic | CNF conversion, Skolemisation, unification, resolution (set-of-support, subsumption) |\n",
        "| Structural-causal-model engine | CounterBench counterfactuals | abduction, do-operator, forward inference |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Run the notebook top to bottom** – every cell only uses functions defined in earlier cells, and the\n",
        "dataset cells degrade gracefully (clear message, no crash) when there is no internet access."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "id": "0a034d3b",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-03T13:42:07.146975Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-03T13:42:07.146853Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-03T13:42:07.152900Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-03T13:42:07.152308Z"
        },
        "id": "0a034d3b"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import re, time, csv, json, heapq, itertools, sys\n",
        "from collections import defaultdict, namedtuple\n",
        "\n",
        "Lit  = namedtuple(\"Lit\", \"neg pred args\")\n",
        "Rule = namedtuple(\"Rule\", \"body head text\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def is_var(t):  return isinstance(t, str) and t.startswith(\"?\")\n",
        "def neg_lit(l): return Lit(not l.neg, l.pred, l.args)\n",
        "def tstr(t):\n",
        "    return f\"{t[0]}({','.join(map(tstr, t[1:]))})\" if isinstance(t, tuple) else str(t)\n",
        "def lit_str(l): return (\"¬\" if l.neg else \"\") + f\"{l.pred}({','.join(map(tstr, l.args))})\"\n",
        "def rule_str(r):\n",
        "    return (\" ∧ \".join(map(lit_str, r.body)) + \" → \" if r.body else \"\") + lit_str(r.head)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
